## 2. Rows skipped, with reason

- **a65 (P3) and b18 (P2) — delete the U+200B lines / characters.** NOT APPLIED. The checker's `blocks`
  check compares the ZWSP count of the Korean source with the target (`ZWSP <src> → <tgt>` = FAIL), and the
  Korean source carries exactly the same zero-width characters (e.g. columns/013 line 34 ends with " ​").
  Removing them fails the gate. Both reviewers themselves identify this as a shared upstream pipeline
  artifact ("no Slovene change", "the same artefact exists in de/fr/cs"). It needs a pipeline-wide fix on
  the Korean source, not a per-locale one.
- **b63 (P2) — join the sentences that are chopped across three paragraphs in 013 and 015.** NOT APPLIED.
  The Korean source has the identical block split, and the `blocks` check compares block counts;
  ACCEPTED-ROUND also lists "requests to merge/split paragraphs" as a skip. Same upstream origin as above.
- **Numeral spell-outs the checker cannot parse.** See §4 — the digit was kept and the sentence repaired
  around it, per the WO instruction "prefer the form the checker accepts and note it in the log".
- **a1 (P1) — delete the dangling ", člen 10" from the 004 source-list label.** APPLIED ONLY IN PART; see §4.
- No row was skipped for a product-fact reason: the consultation lock, the interpreter/reply-time/free-
  consultation/result wording and the gender of attorney Wei Tseng were already correct and were not touched
  except where a row asked for more natural phrasing (b64, a60).

